Hey Snow Plowing Fans!🏂
Today we are officially moving our beta version to the main version - so already every player will have access to the official version without having to load the beta✅

What does version 1.0 introduce compared to version 0.2?🎖️
- added new Truck vehicle 
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/f46645af5c38a9691fa8954ee1591613e245b39d.jpg
- two new ploughs added to vehicles
 {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/d2d016906170060141220bf877a8d8a59c8a50d8.jpg
- added possibility to save at any time - from now on, you will be able to save your game anywhere on the map, except when you are in your vehicle (you will have to leave it for a short save moment). You will be able to save the game from the menu - when you click ESC there will be a 'SAVE GAME' option{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/fefbb1eea38fab631b6da8633703657214fb393a.jpg
- tyre wear on vehicles
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/a9e65677f120c0d0ef2e46a242a2343fe02166c5.jpg
- tool wear;
- wearing out the ploughs;
- wear of clothes;
- improved lighting in the garage
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/44ccfe9273e124308f418af1121c5f17605e23f3.jpg
- addition of additional copyright information to music;
- changed calorie consumption depending on the tool used;
- added tutorials on the consumption of tools, ploughs, clothes and tyres;
- adding collisions that affect the wear and tear of equipment;
- adding the possibility to scrap equipment;
- redesigning the inventory menu so that wear and tear can be checked;
- adding a vehicle icon to the tyre windows;
- Correction of errors in the tyre magazine;
- addition of snowfall on roads and landscape;
- possibility to map 9 binds to tools;
- improved receipt of hut key🗝️
- added additional information that more clearly informs the player that the job of clearing snow from the road has been completed📍
If you haven't played version 1.0 yet, read this post first:
https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/2096030/view/4363510595755124794?l=english
🕵Here are the changes on version 1.0 that you reported to us while playing the beta:🕵

1. improved wearability - reduced wearability of some tools (e.g. snow blower);

2. reduced wearability of all tyres by 50% - It should no longer be the case that clearing snow from the road is unprofitable;

3. repaired truck ramp - it is now possible to drive up on default tyres (however, you need to accelerate and use an appropriate method - we believe you can do it);

4. improvement of the shop and the disposal of used tools - it is no longer possible to deliver an item that the courier does not deliver;

5. repairing the pitch with snow removal along with enlarging the wickets (you can remove the snow with a tractor);

6. repair of an unpleasant error with snow clearing which caused the snow to fill up too quickly, e.g. on the snow bucket (correction of the different snow weight depending on the weather);

7. corrected some collisions with objects;

8. dependence of tyre grip on weather and temperature;

9. improved lamp materials;

10. improved influence of temperature and weather on road and parcel slipperiness.

11. [NEW - added with version 1.0 on general - was not in the beta] We have fixed blueprints that could bug snow removal . Now you shouldn't be in a situation where you can't complete an order at 100%!
For example, where this has been corrected:
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/7113dcd28bf9bab17aa84ae3dc4ed0a73289ceee.jpg
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42941814/690ae88b99144544ec60baa43d28df9e56cf2aa8.jpg
And much more ːthebuilderː


⚠️remember⚠️: If you have the beta version, you must switch to branch general again. All you have to do is change it in Steam library
1. Right click and properties
2. Change from patch 1.0 to NONE.
NOTE - if the game didn't update itself for You, do a Steam relog⚠️ 


